    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 82.40 efficiency score makes him our clear start of the day. Facing Cavalli, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.06 and an elite lead-off spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also earns strong consideration, as his aggressive dynamic platoon advantage against Bassitt significantly boosts his base projection. While **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest matchup of the day against the elite Logan Gilbert (2.98 xERA), his ability to manufacture stolen bases keeps him in the lineup despite the -19% SP skill penalty, as his speed remains the pivot point for our category strategy.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Coby Mayo**, who finished at 44.92. While his raw power profile is enticing, his status as an 8th-order hitter against Cavalli resulted in a negative adjustment that forced him behind **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung**. We are prioritizing order-driven volume today to chase R and RBI, leaving **Coby Mayo** as a high-upside secondary option if **Josh Jung** (51.08) fails to capitalize on his neutral platoon setup. Meanwhile, **Liam Hicks** earns a start at 56.32, with the model favoring his #2 order placement and positive SP skill adjustment over a potential pivot to **Nolan Schanuel**, whose 44.27 score was suppressed by a poor matchup against the southpaw Wrobleski.\n\nManagement is monitoring the lineup integrity for **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas**, both of whom are projected to face the high-contact profile of Taillon. We are essentially betting on their high xwOBA metrics to overcome the park-adjusted ceiling. Note that **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, and with **Kyle Tucker** unavailable, we are missing two high-leverage contributors; consequently, we are relying on **Nasim Nunez** and his switch-hitting flexibility to provide late-game speed, despite his lower total floor. Keep an eye on any weather shifts in the late games, as we are thin on high-ceiling bench depth should we need to scramble.",
